; Two blocks 10 mm apart joined by a flexure (legs 1.5 x 2 x 30, a top bar) and by a rod 0.05 mm square, 8 long, pulled 1 N
; apart. The rod is centred where no line through the samples passes on cells of 1, 0.5 or 0.25 mm (y 0.75, z 1.75), and
; written as the root of a distance, so no sample's tangent plane reaches it (a distance's would, and the samples see it):
; it crossed none of those lines, its stiffness was lost, and the flexure alone read 0.309 mm.
; truth: stiff holds about 0.0152 (statics: the rod's E A / L, 62.5 N/mm, beside the flexure's 3.24 N/mm, 1 N / 0.309 mm read without the rod: 1 N / 65.7 N/mm)
(import "std")
(def a (move (box 2 2 4) 1 1 2))
(def b (move (box 2 2 4) 11 1 2))
(def leg1 (move (box 1.5 2 30) 1.25 1 19))
(def leg2 (move (box 1.5 2 30) 10.75 1 19))
(def top (move (box 11 2 1.5) 6 1 34.25))
(def rod (sqrt (max 0 (move (box 8 0.05 0.05) 6 0.75 1.75))))
(study s (shape (min a b leg1 leg2 top rod)) (elastic (E 200000MPa) (nu 0.3)) (fix root (- x 0.01)) (load end (force 1N 0 0) (region (- 11.9 x))) (res 0.5))
(require stiff (max-displacement s < 0.1))
